00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.212
But when you are the only
attorney in your law firm,

00:02:53.212 --> 00:02:57.150
you live and die by
not only having clients

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.820
but having clients that pay.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:01.290
So its actually very common
for solo practitioners

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:03.310
to get behind on their bills

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:05.030
because not only do the clients

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.060
ebb and flow but also the clients

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.470
ability to pay changes over time.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.940
That's why a lot of law firms of this size

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.880
and even bigger law firms
will get what's called

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:17.150
a line of credit, which
is a revolving loan

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:19.960
that allows them to meet their debts

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:22.080
in lean times and then pay it off

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.620
when the clients come back.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.757
Because obviously you don't want to have

00:03:25.757 --> 00:03:26.590
