00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.620
- So this is obviously very dramatic

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.621
and probably important for the story.

00:04:10.621 --> 00:04:13.360
When the police have probable cause

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.690
to arrest an individual who is suspected

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:18.361
in a capital offense, a felony like this,

00:04:18.361 --> 00:04:21.950
there's no reason to engage
in any kind of pleasantries

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:23.820
or engage in any conversation.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.400
They're going to arrest these two guys

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.340
so there's no point in
having a conversation

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:28.173
with them.

00:04:28.173 --> 00:04:30.120
The proper procedure here would of been

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.310
to avoid the conversation,

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:33.670
go straight to arresting them,

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:35.880
assuming that they have a verified ID

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:37.030
of these two guys

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:38.930
and then give them a Miranda warning

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:40.970
so that whatever they
say can be used against

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:41.850
them at trial.

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:43.730
Right now, since the police officer

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:46.250
has not administered a Miranda warning,

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:47.650
the statements of these individuals

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:48.820
can't be used against them

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:50.720
and won't be admissible in court.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.780
So there's really no point
in taking out your anger

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:54.613
against these guys.

00:04:54.613 --> 00:04:56.080
Just follow proper procedure,

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.220
give them a Miranda warning, arrest them,

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.963
and then get their confessions.

